1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,983
This tutorial follows rent cheques through
Cheque and Cash Collection,

2
00:00:03,983 --> 00:00:07,967
as Maya Khoury, a property manager at
Oasis Crest Properties.

3
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:11,552
Due lists every cheque whose date has
arrived and

4
00:00:11,552 --> 00:00:14,738
that has not cleared yet, across every
property.

5
00:00:14,738 --> 00:00:19,120
Overdue narrows it to cheques past their
grace period, such as

6
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:23,103
Fatima Al Zaabi's May cheque, still
waiting to be banked.

7
00:00:23,103 --> 00:00:27,087
Before a cheque goes to the bank, attach
its photo.

8
00:00:27,087 --> 00:00:31,468
Choose Scan cheques, find the contract,
here Ahmed Hassan's, and continue.

9
00:00:31,468 --> 00:00:34,655
Pick the photo of his October cheque and

10
00:00:34,655 --> 00:00:37,443
extract; reading it takes a few seconds.

11
00:00:37,443 --> 00:00:41,427
Miftah reads the cheque number, the bank,
the payer, the

12
00:00:41,427 --> 00:00:45,012
date and the amount, and matches it to
cheque

13
00:00:45,012 --> 00:00:48,597
5 on his contract, dated the first of
October.

14
00:00:48,597 --> 00:00:52,182
Check the row and approve: the scan is
attached.

15
00:00:52,182 --> 00:00:54,572
To deposit is where banking starts.

16
00:00:54,572 --> 00:00:58,555
Tick the cheques going to the bank today:
Ahmed Hassan's

17
00:00:58,555 --> 00:01:02,538
200104 and Fatima's 300204, both dated the
first of October.

18
00:01:02,538 --> 00:01:06,123
The selected total, 36,750, should match
the deposit slip.

19
00:01:06,123 --> 00:01:08,912
Deposit Batch records both as deposited
today,

20
00:01:08,912 --> 00:01:11,700
each into its own property's bank account.

21
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:14,489
When the bank confirms a cheque has

22
00:01:14,489 --> 00:01:17,277
cleared, find it in the Cheque register.

23
00:01:17,277 --> 00:01:20,065
Ahmed's July cheque, 200103, is still
deposited.

24
00:01:20,065 --> 00:01:24,049
Choose Clear, check the account it cleared
into, and confirm.

25
00:01:24,049 --> 00:01:28,032
It is now Cleared, with its receipt number
beside it.

26
00:01:28,032 --> 00:01:29,625
Not every cheque clears.

27
00:01:29,625 --> 00:01:31,617
Fatima's 300204 comes back unpaid.

28
00:01:31,617 --> 00:01:34,405
Choose Bounce, pick the reason the bank

29
00:01:34,405 --> 00:01:36,795
gave, here Payment stopped, and confirm.

30
00:01:36,795 --> 00:01:40,380
Miftah records the return, proposes the
contract's cheque-return charge

31
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:43,965
of 1,000 for approval, and asks what
happens next.

32
00:01:43,965 --> 00:01:45,160
Choose Replace now.

33
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:49,144
Fatima hands over a new cheque for the
full 15,500.

34
00:01:49,144 --> 00:01:51,932
Enter its number, 300295, its date, the

35
00:01:51,932 --> 00:01:54,322
fifteenth of October, and its bank.

36
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:58,704
The replacements cover the whole amount,
so nothing is left owing.

37
00:01:58,704 --> 00:01:59,102
Replace.

38
00:01:59,102 --> 00:02:03,882
The Post-dated view lists the cheques
maturing in the next two weeks

39
00:02:03,882 --> 00:02:08,264
with a running total, and Fatima's new
cheque is already there.

40
00:02:08,264 --> 00:02:11,450
The same story is on each tenancy
contract.

41
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:15,434
On Ahmed's Cheques tab, 200103 is now
Cleared, and 200104

42
00:02:15,434 --> 00:02:19,019
is Deposited, with the bank read from its
scan.

43
00:02:19,019 --> 00:02:22,205
Nothing is ever deleted: every cheque
stays traceable,

44
00:02:22,205 --> 00:02:25,392
from registered to deposited, cleared,
returned or replaced.
